## 💣 13. The 14 Shopify Theme Engineering Landmines (Reliability & Importer Sync Checklist)
For complete implementation details and AST auto-fix patterns, refer to `references/shopify_reliability_landmines_and_importer_sync_guide.md`.
1. **Forbidden `{% stylesheet %}` / `{% javascript %}` Tags**: Shopify's cloud theme importer silently drops sections containing these tags. Always use external asset files or scoped `{% style %}`.
2. **Block Name Length <= 25 Characters**: Shopify Theme Customizer truncates or errors out on schema block names exceeding 25 characters. Keep them concise.
3. **Color Scheme Group Role Keys**: `config/settings_schema.json` with `color_scheme_group` requires exact role keys (`text`, `background`, `solid_button_labels`, etc.).
4. **Static Section Tags in Layout**: Never use static `{% section 'header' %}` in layout files. Use section groups `{% sections 'header-group' %}` so merchants can customize via admin.
5. **No Filters Inside `image_tag` Parameters**: Liquid parameters in `image_tag` cannot contain pipe filters (e.g. `width: settings.width | default: 800` is invalid). Assign variables beforehand.
6. **Missing Defaults on Required Schema Settings**: Always specify `"default"` values in section/block schema settings to prevent null references during initial render.
7. **Font Picker Settings Without `font_face` Loader**: Using `type: "font_picker"` requires `{{ settings.font | font_face: font_display: 'swap' }}` in `<head>`.
8. **Hardcoded Currencies / Raw Price Numbers**: Never print raw price integers or hardcode dollar signs. Always pass through `money` or `money_with_currency` Liquid filters.
9. **CSS Color Opacity & Design Tokens**: Expose design token colors as space-separated RGB triplets (`--color-surface: 24 24 27;`) and consume via `rgb(var(--color-surface) / <opacity>)`.
10. **Image Responsive Sizing & CLS Prevention**: Always provide explicit `width` and `height` attributes alongside responsive `srcset` and `sizes` to eliminate Cumulative Layout Shift.
11. **App Block Embed Target `content_for_header`**: `layout/theme.liquid` must always contain `{{ content_for_header }}` in `<head>` for app injections and scripts to load.
12. **Comment Headers in ANY JSON File (`templates/*.json`, `config/`, `locales/`) Forbidden**: Shopify's Theme Importer requires strict RFC 8259 JSON. C-style comment headers (e.g. `/* IMPORTANT: The contents of this file are auto-generated... */`) silently drop template registration in the Theme Editor, throwing `"No templates found for products"`. Always strip `/* ... */` comments prior to ZIP packaging.
13. **Two-Phase Schema Mutation Invariant**: Never update `{% schema %}` and `templates/*.json` in a single combined patch. Ship schema definitions in `.liquid` first, then reference them in `.json`.
14. **Section Schema `range` Step & Bound Violations (`step must evenly divide the range`)**: Schema settings of type `"range"` strictly require `(max - min) % step === 0`. Violating this (e.g. `min: 0, max: 59, step: 5` where remainder is 4) throws `FileSaveError: setting with id="..." step must evenly divide the range` in the Theme Editor / CLI and causes HTTP 422 drops during ZIP import. Always verify `(max - min) % step == 0` (e.g. `0..55` with step 5). Values in `settings_data.json` or templates exceeding `min`/`max` or non-multiples of `step` trigger similar drops.
15. **Theme Customizer Inspector Interception on Drawers**: Theme Editor inspect mode fires `event.preventDefault()` on preview clicks. Drawer scripts that return on `event.defaultPrevented` fail to open in customizer; guard with `window.Shopify?.designMode` bypass and handle `shopify:block:select` on header cart blocks.
16. **Theme Upgrade Schema Translation Drops**: Upgrading third-party themes (e.g. v3.7 -> v4.0) often corrupts or truncates `locales/*.schema.json`, causing `Missing translation:` errors across customizer blocks. Reconcile missing `t:...` keys against `sections/`, `blocks/`, and prior theme version archives.
17. **Liquid Validator `elsif` Regex Boundary**: When auditing Liquid tag balance, regex patterns matching `{% if` must assert a negative lookahead `(?!else|elsif)` so intermediate conditional branches are not miscounted as opening tags.
18. **Theme Block Snippet Scope & Section Object Isolation**: In Shopify OS 2.0 Theme Blocks (`blocks/*.liquid`), calling `{% render 'snippet' %}` does NOT automatically pass the parent `section` object. If the snippet targets `{{ section.id }}` (e.g. `#ProductSubmitButton-{{ section.id }}`), `section.id` evaluates to empty string, silently breaking unique ID selectors in CSS/JS. Always explicitly pass `section: section` in render calls, and back ID selectors with robust class selectors (`.product-form__submit`, `.atc-button`).
19. **Conditional Schema Visibility (`visible_if`) & Fallback Cascade Pitfall**: Hiding core layout controls behind conditions (e.g. `"visible_if": "{{ block.settings.atc_label_2 != blank }}"`) completely hides the slider in the Customizer when the condition is unmet and often causes liquid templates to skip styling. Core dimensions (e.g. button vertical padding / height) must remain unconditionally accessible, paired with a robust 3-tier Liquid fallback: `assign pad = block.settings.atcbuttonpadding | default: block.settings.atc_button_padding_y | default: 20`.
20. **ATC Button Vertical Padding & Quantity Selector Flex Stretch**: When increasing Add to Cart (ATC) button height via vertical padding, adjacent quantity selectors in flex rows (`.product-form__quantity-and-btn`) become vertically misaligned or shrunken. Ensure the flex container specifies `align-items: stretch` and the quantity input/wrapper enforces `height: 100% !important; min-height: 100% !important;` so both controls scale in lockstep.
21. **Canonical Root Template Requirement for Custom Templates (`No templates found for products`)**: In Shopify OS 2.0, all custom templates (`templates/product.*.json`) strictly require the base canonical root template (`templates/product.json` or `templates/product.liquid`). If `product.json` is missing or discarded by the importer due to comment/schema errors, Shopify's template indexing breaks completely: the customizer dropdown displays `"No templates found for products"`, `+ Create template` disappears, custom templates become orphaned, and product URLs 404. Always ensure `templates/product.json` is present with valid schema.
22. **Theme Customizer Dropdown Desync & Live Preview Click-Through Navigation**: When the customizer top search dropdown modal fails to list product templates due to admin indexing lag on draft themes, navigate by clicking directly on any product card in the live canvas preview iframe; the editor automatically catches the event and opens the product's template.
23. **Theme ZIP Upload Forking (New Theme ID) vs Stale Browser Tab Desync & In-Place Code Editor Recovery**: Uploading a `.zip` archive via `Online Store > Themes > Add theme` creates a brand new theme with a fresh theme ID. Continuing to edit the old draft theme in an already-open browser tab will inspect stale files where `product.json` was missing. Either switch to the newly created theme in the Themes library or perform instant in-place recovery on the active theme via `... > Edit code > Add a new template > Product (JSON) > product` and paste the clean `product.json` directly.
24. **Theme Blocks 2.0 Inverted Block Hierarchy & Container Delegation (`{% content_for 'blocks' %}`)**: In modern Shopify themes (e.g. Shrine Theme, Horizon, Dawn 15+ Theme Blocks architecture), `sections/main-product.liquid` no longer contains a monolithic `{%- case block.type -%}` loop or giant block schemas. Instead, `main-product.liquid` delegates layout via `{% content_for 'block', id: 'details', type: 'main-product_details' %}`, and `blocks/main-product_details.liquid` renders children via `{% content_for 'blocks' %}`. Attempting to inject new block cases or block schemas into `main-product.liquid` has zero effect or fails schema validation. Instead: (1) create the standalone block file in `blocks/<block-handle>.liquid` with its own `{% schema %}`, (2) register `{"type": "<block-handle>"}` inside the `"blocks"` array of `blocks/main-product_details.liquid` (and any other container blocks like `sections/featured-product.liquid`), and (3) in `templates/product.json`, place the block instance inside `blocks[details].blocks` and `blocks[details].block_order`, NOT at the root section block level.
25. **Experimental Theme Blocks Importer Rejection vs Monolithic OS 2.0 Standardization**: When themes use experimental Theme Blocks (`blocks/` directory, nested blocks inside container blocks without a top-level `block_order` on `sections.main`), production Shopify stores lacking the developer preview flag will fail JSON schema validation during ZIP import and silently discard `templates/product.json`, triggering `"No templates found for products"`. See `references/shopify_theme_blocks_importer_pitfalls.md` for full diagnosis, instant in-admin recovery, and the standard DNK monolithic OS 2.0 flat-blocks migration pattern.
26. **Dynamic Button Height in Modern Theme Blocks (ATC + Dynamic Checkout + Quantity Sync)**: When adding customizable button height settings (e.g., `button_height` and `button_height_mobile` range settings) in `blocks/product_buy-buttons.liquid`, styling only `.product-form__submit` causes a visual desync with Shopify Dynamic Checkout buttons (`.shopify-payment-button__button`, `[role="button"]`) which stay fixed at theme default (`4.6rem` in `base.css`). The generated CSS in `snippets/buy-buttons.liquid` must target: (a) main ATC `#ProductSubmitButton-{{ section.id }}` / `.product-form__submit`, (b) secondary skip-cart buttons `#SectionAtcBtn-{{ section.id }}`, (c) dynamic payment buttons `.shopify-payment-button__button` & `.shopify-payment-button__button--unbranded`, and (d) adjacent row quantity selectors `.product-form__quantity-and-btn .quantity`. Ensure range schema settings adhere to `(max - min) % step === 0` (e.g. 36..100 step 1 px), include mobile media query `@media screen and (max-width: 749px)`, and ensure Liquid AST validators support hyphenated trimming delimiters (`{%-?` / `-?%`) to avoid false-positive unbalanced tag warnings. See `references/shrine_buy_buttons_height_and_liquid_whitespace_ast.md` for full implementation and AST patterns.
27. **Shopify Schema Text Settings "default can't be blank" Invariant**: In Shopify `{% schema %}`, settings of `"type": "text"` or `"type": "textarea"` strictly forbid `"default": ""`. If declared, the Shopify Theme Editor and Admin JSON parser reject the file with `FileSaveError: Invalid schema: setting with id="..." default can't be blank`. If an optional text setting should default to empty/blank, **completely omit the `"default"` key** from the schema object. Handle fallbacks downstream in Liquid via `| default: ...`. See `references/shopify_cro_shipping_countdown_estimator_playbook.md` (Pitfalls 14–17).
28. **Shopify Schema Select Option Label Max Length (50 Characters) & Visual Row Order**: In Shopify section/block `{% schema %}`, every option in a `select` setting strictly enforces `label.length <= 50`. Exceeding 50 characters (e.g. adding descriptive examples inside option labels) triggers `FileSaveError: Invalid schema: setting with id="..." option label is too long (max 50 characters)`. Keep option labels short and concise (e.g., "Before flag", "After flag") and place visual hints into the setting's `"info"` attribute. In multi-row widgets, arrange schema settings to align with the visual row flow in storefront preview (e.g. place `order_text` / timer prefix directly before the `header` for delivery dates range). See `references/shopify_cro_shipping_countdown_estimator_playbook.md` (Pitfall 18).
29. **Liquid Schema JSON Trailing Commas & AST Double-Parse Validation Invariant**: In Shopify `{% schema %}` blocks, JSON syntax is strictly enforced. Hand-written or LLM-synthesized JSON frequently leaves trailing commas (e.g. `[1, 2,]` or `{"a": 1,}`), which standard JSON parsers and Shopify's cloud uploader reject. When building Theme Blocks, always extract all `{% schema %}...{% endschema %}` blocks and validate with strict `json.loads()`, and assert that Liquid pairing tags (`{% if %}`/`{% endif %}`, `{% unless %}`/`{% endunless %}`) are strictly balanced.
30. **CSS `@layer cro-blocks` Specificity & Zero-Conflict Token Inheritance**: In Shopify themes using conflicting global CSS resets or Tailwind, atomic CRO theme blocks must wrap styles within `@layer cro-blocks { ... }` while exposing `--cro-*` CSS Custom Properties on the custom element host. This prevents theme stylesheets from overriding block layouts while allowing clean inheritance of `--font-body-family`, `--color-accent`, and global radius tokens without resorting to `!important`.
31. **Shopify Native `Українська (Бета-версія)` Admin Locale & Dual-Layer `uk.schema.json` Binding (Zero-Weight-Claim Gate)**: Never claim from stale LLM training data that Shopify Admin does not support Ukrainian or cannot load `locales/uk.schema.json`. Shopify Account (`accounts.shopify.com/.../personal` -> *Manage account -> Preferred language*) natively supports **`Українська (Бета-версія)`**. When selected, Shopify Admin initializes the Theme Customizer with the `uk` locale and natively loads `locales/uk.schema.json` (translating all section, block, and theme setting labels without touching `en.default.schema.json`). Concurrently, storefront localization (`Settings -> Languages -> Українська (Україна)`) loads `locales/uk.json`. Always verify platform locale/feature support against live official Shopify documentation or the user's open session before asserting platform limitations.
32. **Multi-Line `console.log()` Regex Truncation (`SyntaxError` in `assets/global.js`) & Mandatory `node --check` Gate**: Never strip multi-line CSS-styled `console.log('%c...', 'color: #ff8800; font-weight: bold;...')` calls with single-line `[^;]*\);` regexes—stopping at the first `;` inside a CSS string literal leaves dangling lines (`SyntaxError: Unexpected token ':'`) that abort `assets/global.js`, breaking `removeTrapFocus()` in `SideDrawer.close()` (causing drawers/modals to freeze open) and preventing `<recently-viewed-products>` registration. Also never use escaped `\.` inside regex replacement strings on `.liquid`/`.json` files (`Invalid \escape` in `{% schema %}`). Always run `scripts/audit_commercial_theme_zip.py` (which enforces `node --check` on all `.js` and `{% javascript %}` blocks plus `json.loads` on all `.json` and `{% schema %}` blocks) before sealing any theme ZIP.
33. **`<side-drawer>` Attribute Completeness & `RecentlyViewedProducts` Defer Race / Self-Splice Bugs (Ella 7.x / Horizon)**: Ensure every `<side-drawer>` includes `id="Drawer-Overlay-..."`, `data-drawer-content`, and `data-drawer-direction` (and guard `this.overlay?.closest('details')` + `typeof removeTrapFocus === 'function'` in `SideDrawer.close()`). For floating `#popup-recently-viewed` drawers: (a) do not splice the current `data-product-id` out of `_halo_recently_viewed` (otherwise viewing 1 product renders `"Sorry, there are no products"`), (b) synchronously record `product-info[data-product-id]` inside `RecentlyViewedProducts` to prevent `<head defer>` (`global.js`) vs `<body defer>` (`product-info.js`) load-order races, and (c) bypass `IntersectionObserver` on hidden drawers (`visibility: hidden`) and refresh on `SideDrawer.open()`. See `references/shopify_theme_debranding_and_proprietary_adaptation_playbook.md` (§9.3).
34. **Mutual Watchdog Mesh, Silent Cart Quantity Sabotage & Zero-Hex (`_0x = 0`) Deobfuscation (Shrine Pro 1.9.0 / Ascendify 2.10.0)**: In heavily obfuscated commercial themes (`Shrine Pro`, `Ascendify`), removing the primary license fetch in `global.js` triggers secondary cross-file watchdogs disguised as standard assets (`assets/cart-functions.js`, `assets/header-icons.js`, `assets/header-drawer-icons.js`, `assets/footer-form.js`) that monkey-patch `window.fetch` and wipe `<main>` 3–5 seconds after `DOMContentLoaded` if license endpoints were not called or returned mocked `403 Blocked`. Additionally, check `assets/kit-fontawesome.js` and `assets/global.js` for silent cart sabotage (injecting `<input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="<random 0..10>">` into `<product-form>` or calling `.remove()` on `.atc-button, .cart__checkout-button` when `settings.icon_fav` is blank), and audit `snippets/` (`cart-items-data.liquid`, `footer-data.liquid`, `section-previews.liquid`, `meta-tags.liquid`) for inline obfuscated lockout screens. Reconstruct clean source (`_0x count = 0`) using Node `vm` string-array evaluation, proxy-dictionary inlining, and Rosetta-Stone AST alignment against clean baseline versions (`CLEAR JS Shrine Pro 1.3.2`). Full 14-layer neutralization matrix: `references/shopify_js_deobfuscation_and_mutual_watchdog_neutralization.md`.


